## Design: Per-Node Failure Mode Syntax (Phase 2.6)

**Branch:** `feat/14-per-node-failure-mode-syntax`  
**Design doc:** [`docs/design/0014-per-node-failure-mode-syntax.md`](https://github.com/vertexrs-io/vertexrs/blob/feat/14-per-node-failure-mode-syntax/docs/design/0014-per-node-failure-mode-syntax.md)

> ⚠️ Automated draft PR creation is blocked by repo permissions. Please open the draft PR manually: `feat/14-per-node-failure-mode-syntax` → `main`.

---

### Approach

Sigils and `pure` are handled entirely in the `pipeline!` macro code-generation layer. The standalone `node!` macro is unchanged; unannotated nodes emit the same code as today — no overhead.

1. `pipeline!` parser now calls `parse_node_item_meta` instead of storing raw tokens.
2. Sigil detection: `?` is parsed by syn as `Expr::Try`; `!` is left unconsumed after `Expr::parse` and then peeked. `, pure = false` follows a trailing comma.
3. Sigil-carrying nodes are wrapped in `std::panic::catch_unwind` in the generated `run()` body.

---

### Files Changed

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `vertexrs/src/lib.rs` | `Node<T>` gains `validity: Option<NullBuffer>` and `pure: bool`; new `all_na`, `null_count`, `with_pure`; `BoolNode` gains `pure` + `with_pure`; `AnyNode::null_count`; `Frame::null_count` |
| `vertexrs-macro/src/lib.rs` | `NodeFailureOverride` enum; `NodeItemMeta` struct; `parse_node_item_meta` fn; `OrderedItem::Node` → `Box<NodeItemMeta>`; three new `ord_run` code-gen branches |

---

### Key Signatures

```rust
// Node<T> — two new public fields
pub struct Node<T: ArrowNativeType> {
    pub name:     &'static str,
    pub deps:     &'static [&'static str],
    pub data:     ScalarBuffer<T>,
    pub validity: Option<arrow_buffer::NullBuffer>,  // None = all valid
    pub pure:     bool,                               // false = always-dirty
}

// New methods on Node<T>
pub fn all_na(name: &'static str, deps: &'static [&'static str], len: usize) -> Self;
pub fn null_count(&self) -> usize;
pub fn with_pure(mut self, pure: bool) -> Self;

// Frame helper
pub fn null_count(&self, name: &str) -> Option<usize>;

// Macro-internal
struct NodeItemMeta {
    name:             Ident,
    receiver_ident:   Option<Ident>,          // for NA fallback .len()
    core_expr_tokens: proc_macro2::TokenStream, // name = expr, no sigil/pure
    failure_override: NodeFailureOverride,     // None | Soft | Hard
    pure:             bool,
}
```

---

### Generated Code (in `run()`)

**Soft failure (`?`):**
```rust
let tax = match ::std::panic::catch_unwind(::std::panic::AssertUnwindSafe(|| {
    use vertexrs::{Node, BoolNode, ColRef};
    vertexrs::node!(tax = price.row(|_x| -> f64 { panic!("oops") }));
    tax
})) {
    Ok(__n) => __n,
    Err(__e) => {
        let __msg = /* extract panic payload as String */;
        self.__warnings.push(format!("node 'tax': kernel failed: {}", __msg));
        vertexrs::Node::all_na("tax", &[], price.len())
    }
};
```

**Hard failure (`!`):**
```rust
let tax = ::std::panic::catch_unwind(::std::panic::AssertUnwindSafe(|| {
    use vertexrs::{Node, BoolNode, ColRef};
    vertexrs::node!(tax = price.row(|_x| -> f64 { panic!("oops") }));
    tax
})).map_err(|__e| {
    vertexrs::PipelineError::KernelPanic(format!("node 'tax': {}", __msg))
})?;
```

**`pure = false`:**
```rust
vertexrs::node!(counter = src.row(|x| x + 1.0));
let counter = counter.with_pure(false);
```

---

### ADR Impact

No new ADR required. ADR-0005 explicitly anticipates macro updates for new execution modes. ADR-0001 is satisfied by using `arrow_buffer::NullBuffer` for validity.

### Known Limitation

`BoolNode` soft-failure NA is not fully specified. Implementer should add `BoolNode::all_na` or restrict `?`/`!` sigils to non-bool nodes with a compile error for bool nodes with sigils.

---

**Ready for human sign-off.** Review the design in the linked doc on branch `feat/14-per-node-failure-mode-syntax`, then set the `design-approved` label on this issue to trigger the Implementer, who will pick up the branch and complete the implementation.
